# Component Development Rules

## 🧩 Component Structure Standards

### Component Template Structure

```typescript
import React from "react";
import { ComponentProps } from "./ComponentType";
import * as S from "./style/Component.style";

interface ComponentProps {
  // Define props with proper types
}

function Component({ prop1, prop2 }: ComponentProps) {
  // Hooks first
  // Business logic
  // Event handlers
  // Render
  return <S.Container>{/* JSX */}</S.Container>;
}

export default Component;
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** create separate style files for components
✅ **ALWAYS** use proper TypeScript interfaces for props
✅ **ALWAYS** destructure props in function parameters
✅ **ALWAYS** use semantic HTML elements
✅ **ALWAYS** handle loading and error states
✅ **ALWAYS** use React.memo for expensive components
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper accessibility (aria-labels, roles)
✅ **ALWAYS** use styled-components with theme integration

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** use inline styles or className strings
❌ **NEVER** create components without proper TypeScript types
❌ **NEVER** forget to export components as default
❌ **NEVER** use div for semantic elements (use section, article, etc.)
❌ **NEVER** forget error boundaries for complex components
❌ **NEVER** use any type for props or state

